# Security headers for the OEdu app: edu.oplocloud.com and kern.oplocloud.com,
# which publish this one directory (wrangler.toml, wrangler.kern.toml).
#
# Cloudflare reads this file at deploy and applies it to every asset answer,
# including the ones worker/index.js hands back from env.ASSETS for /admin/,
# /teacher/ and /student/. Nothing here changes what a page does: each line
# only turns off something the app never uses. The sign-in page
# (auth.oplocloud.com) and OC EFM (efm/_headers) already send this set.
#
#   nosniff        a file is read as the type it was served as, never guessed
#   frame-ancestors / X-Frame-Options
#                  no page may frame the app, so it cannot be clickjacked.
#                  Nothing in this repository frames it.
#   Permissions-Policy
#                  the app uses no camera, microphone, location or payment API
#   HSTS           the hostnames are https-only; a year, no preload
#
# Not here, on purpose: a Content-Security-Policy that restricts scripts. The
# app is built on inline scripts and handlers, so a strict policy would blank
# it. That needs the inline code moved into files first; until then
# frame-ancestors is the only directive that is safe to send.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
